note Drag the sash between two panels to move the boundary between them; the cursor shows the resize arrows while hovering or dragging. The reader reaches for it to give the room to whichever panel matters now, a wide graph or a tall outline, instead of an even split. The position is kept as a share of the split, so it follows the window when the window is resized, and each side keeps a floor of 12 columns across or 4 rows down. The new share is saved with the layout once the sash is let go.

